{
  "_why": "Role track for MAINTENANCE TECHNICIAN, authored under docs/profiling/role-pack-authoring-guide.md as Batch 2 part two's seventh and last pack. The generic packs it sits beside stay exactly as they are: fam_fitting keeps ISCO unit 7233 and fam_machinery_repair keeps minor 723 for everybody this family does not bind. It shipped only once ruling A1 could be carried out -- plain 'fitter' retired off 7233.0101 Maintenance Fitter-Mechanical (rvm-alias-retirements.jsonl) and moved to Bench Fitter -- so that code could leave the Fitter's interim binding and come here. fam_maintenance_tech binds its NCO occupations directly (job_domain specificity 50 beats unit 40 and minor 30).",
  "_scope": "PLANT MAINTENANCE -- keeping a factory's machines running: mechanical, hydraulic, pneumatic and basic electrical, preventive and breakdown, from maintenance helper to senior technician. The level ladder (Helper / Technician / Senior Technician) is asked as maintenance_level so the sheet can say which rung the man stands on. Vehicle workshops (fam_auto_mechanic), building and AC maintenance, telephone and electronics repair, and pure electrical maintenance (Industrial Electrician) are not bound here; the family row in _families.jsonl records each.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS maintenance_experience, asked FIRST, and it is MAINTENANCE_TECHNICIAN.tenureQuestionKey. It cannot be experience_years from qp_universal: phase order runs occupation_specific BEFORE universal_tail, so the universal answer does not exist yet when these items are selected -- gating on it is permanently false. Its options carry value_number ONLY. pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, so a value_text beside the number would turn every gte gate below into a string comparison that is false forever.",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 48 and qp_universal@4 spends at most 18. Tier 0 is 7 items, tier 1 (maintenance_experience >= 2) adds 3, tier 2 (>= 5) adds 3 -- a senior walks 13, two fewer than the welder's 15, and 13 + 18 = 31 against the ceiling of 48. The three fresher items are gated maintenance_experience <= 0, so a senior never sees them and a fresher, who fails both gte gates by construction, tops out at 7 + 3 = 10.",
  "_sheet": "SECTION B IS READ OFF THE RATIFIED MAINTENANCE REFERENCE RESUME (Arif Khan, Maintenance Technician -- Senior Technician, page 10), not invented. Its eight rows are Disciplines, Equipment maintained, Maintenance type, Instruments & tools, Drawings, Response worked to, Documentation and Sector worked, and every one has a question here that fills it. Maintenance type and Instruments & tools carry SIX values plus the escape chip because the page prints six in each. Equipment keeps the page's 'CNC machines' as a chip: the descriptor deliberately does NOT make it a machine term (a CNC operator says it about the machine he runs), but a pack chip is never routing evidence -- it is only served to a worker whose family already resolved here. Response time is a BANDED single_select, the welder's plate ruling. ONE CELL IS NOT REPRODUCED VERBATIM: the page's Documentation row is prose ('Maintains PM checklists, breakdown log and MTTR record'); the pack asks which records the man keeps, and the row prints them ' · '-joined. This pack has no case in role-sheet-parity.render.test.ts yet.",
  "_keys": "NO DIGITS IN ANY question_key OR option_key. Both regexes are ^[a-z_]+$, and slugKey REFUSES a key with a digit at runtime -- which is why the response bands are within_fifteen / within_thirty and not within_30. measuring_tools, drawing_reading and sector_worked are the SHARED keys other packs already use, deliberately: resume-degradation.ts sheds rows BY KEY (sector_worked first) to keep a sheet on one page, and a private key would opt this trade out of that.",
  "pack_id": "qp_maintenance_tech",
  "version": 2,
  "family_id": "fam_maintenance_tech",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "v2 (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #5): Easy/Medium/Advanced tiers; 6-band experience; sheet-21 level ladder (Helper/Trainee, Technician, Senior technician, Supervisor / maintenance in-charge; now mandatory; the first chip stores `trainee`, Turner @6 precedent, and old `helper` answers still render) + 1 separating confirm for senior_technician, the sheet's question verbatim (the only rung above it is supervisor, by rule); Medium Q6 machine type (+conventional machines, +injection moulding machines, +boilers, +packaging machines; CNC/VMC, compressors/utilities and conveyors/cranes relabelled to the sheet's words) and Q7 systems (+lubrication, +welding/fabrication for repair); Advanced NEW Q9 CNC-specific row (spindle, ATC, ball-screw, backlash, alarms), Q10 PM/TPM/CMMS (+TPM on the work row, +CMMS on the record row), NEW Q11 utilities row (compressor, chiller, boiler licence, ETP); maintenance type, instruments and drawing retagged Advanced; depth rows gated years OR rung (senior technician and up). Deviations recorded: hydraulic power packs / pumps & blowers machine chips kept as history (append-only); no shift row and no per-trade ITI row (Q12 is the shared qp_universal block, Track A/B precedent). Drafted for owner review (Prakash).",
  "_fresher": "Guideline section 11 #1: a fresher's Zone 4 is training, trade test, machines used in the ITI workshop and project work, and the History heading never renders empty. These three items are the ask half; resume-fresher-rows.ts, fed by this role's descriptor, is the render half. The KEYS are read literally by that file and must not be renamed; only the workshop VOCABULARY is trade-specific (the page's worker came through ITI Mechanic Machine Tool Maintenance). The three prompts are the welder's verbatim, so they reuse its served text and its voice clips.",
